# netsurf: decline the local block insert/remove path on structural selectors
#
# Roadmap WS-C, script-driven DOM changes. Patch 166's html_rl_block_change
# locally removes/inserts block boxes and calls layout_relayout_block, but
# the existing parent, sibling and ancestor boxes keep styles selected
# before the DOM mutation. Any of these selector dependencies can change
# state on insert/remove while this path never reselects them:
#   :first-child, :last-child, :nth-child(), :nth-last-child(),
#   :only-child, :only-of-type, :first-of-type, :last-of-type,
#   :nth-of-type(), :nth-last-of-type(), :empty, :has(), and the sibling
#   combinators + and ~.
#
# Concrete repro:  CSS p:first-child { margin-top: 0 }. Insert a new first
# <p>: the new block gets fresh margin-top:0, but the old first block keeps
# its stale 0 instead of becoming 1em, and patch 166's margin comparison
# can then accept stale-equals-fresh and report success with geometry one
# margin off -- a silent divergence, not a crash.
#
# Fix: a minimal conservative selector-dependency gate, reusing patch 186's
# per-stylesheet analysis. The compound parser now records a structural
# bitmask (positional / :empty / :has) on every compound; the sheet cache
# keeps the list alongside the sibling-combinator state. html_rl_block_change
# calls html_rl_block_structural_risk after confirming a change exists but
# before touching any box: if a used sheet needs the conservative check
# (patch-186 state 2), has sibling combinators (state 1), or holds a
# structural compound whose static parts could match an affected element
# (positional -> any sibling; :empty -> the parent; :has() -> the parent or
# an ancestor), the change declines and the existing full reconversion runs
# on the untouched tree. Structural pseudo-classes inside :not()/:is()/
# /:where() also decline (they are evaluated against the element itself);
# inside :has() they are dropped (the outer :has bit covers the ancestor).
# Unparseable relevant syntax declines via the existing r=2 path.
#
# Decline conditions (any one): sheet state 2; sheet state 1 (any +/~);
# a positional compound statically matching a sibling element; an :empty
# compound statically matching the parent element; a :has compound
# statically matching the parent or an ancestor box's element; any DOM
# error while walking (cannot prove safety).
#
# Measurements: full simulator gate (VM, 2026-10-01). DOMSTALL 9/9 (new
# step 8: insert a new first div into #probe under
# #probe div:first-child{margin-top:0}; the insert declines -- engine log
# shows "structural selector may restyle a sibling" -- and the full layout
# gives the old first div its 1em top margin back: ~16px gap to the
# inserted div, asserted geometrically). Engine log for the page: 4 local
# text rebuilds, 3 local block placements (the 5000-p steps keep the local
# path: div:first-child cannot match <p> siblings, span:empty cannot match
# the div parent), 1 structural decline. BLOCKSIB 3/3, SIB186 6/6,
# EVORDER 5/5, SELECTORS 85/85.
#
# The patch-163 gap (layout_relayout_block not scanning earlier siblings
# for a positioned descendant whose containing block is a grown ancestor)
# is intentionally left out: reusing lr_subtree_unsafe on the prev chains
# newly declines on pages with fixed-position earlier siblings (the
# dom-stall page's own #res header), which would zero the ds_blocks gate
# count. A precise bottom-anchor check needs new ancestor-aware logic and
# does not fit cleanly here; it stays a follow-up.
#
# Test: testpages/pages/JS-dom-stall.html step 8 (CSS + #probe fixture +
# geometric assert); tools/run-vita-sim.sh now expects DOMSTALL 9/9, >= 3
# local block placements, and >= 1 structural decline on the page.
#
